From 243f1413d6cb95d8403f56cb5f20fbf974b33e03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:12:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/35] nas-relay: pause I/Q to the Tab5 from TX; to RX;

The incoming I/Q (~190 KB/s) is what overflows the Tab5's WiFi SDIO link
during a burst; on 2026-10-14 one such stall held the last symbols back by
1.5 s. PINGs continue, so the Tab5's 3 s idle timeout is not tripped; a
pause ends after 180 s even without RX;. Flag file iq-during-tx keeps
streaming, for A/B tests. The transmit log records the mode per burst and
tx_compare.py groups the result by it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
